de is $|A|.$\n\nSince $A=-7,$ we have that the amplitude is $|A|=|-7|=7.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253368 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aadff32-d8e0-5eea-8f1f-2f63a134c39f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250649} {:answer/id #uuid "3acd747a-676c-53ac-a0b1-66a6584544d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251041} {:answer/id #uuid "535dc4a7-779d-5aa4-84ff-894b2006269b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251232} {:answer/id #uuid "dfcaf382-661a-5eed-a5ae-ca4d55214483" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252528} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d7f858-fa72-532e-b037-12bd5a63a44f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "535dc4a7-779d-5aa4-84ff-894b2006269b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251232} :answer-field/id #uuid "367782f4-ca15-5206-b0f9-015103d3f79a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252895}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86dec134-c288-5f12-9971-6b0570d7076d" :question/math-academy-id "q-117576" :question/problem "What is the amplitude of the function $f(x)=\\frac{3-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{5}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that we can rewrite the function as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{5}=-\\frac{9}{5}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, given a function in the form $f(x)=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the amplitude is $|A|.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $A=-\\frac{9}{5}.$ Therefore, the amplitude is $|A|=|-\\frac{9}{5}|=\\frac{9}{5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 175921863328