rm $y=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=\\frac{3}{4}.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{(\\frac{3}{4})}=\\frac{8\\pi }{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71fbeca3-4760-5d6a-856c-a573ea317eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{300}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251486} {:answer/id #uuid "9229fa93-9ffb-5473-9b2e-ff4e454a6679" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{270}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251803} {:answer/id #uuid "ca888844-ac33-5b63-a641-8bce7947f0cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{480}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252347} {:answer/id #uuid "f2fdabb1-db44-594d-8452-62e77cc9289f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252685} {:answer/id #uuid "fc9b6765-ab75-54b3-a097-f8617bfd508d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{120}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9229fa93-9ffb-5473-9b2e-ff4e454a6679" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{270}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251803} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf475618-9da6-5ade-89c7-309940393d4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253135}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e0d5cec2-04d5-542c-903e-28cdf3f5b313" :question/math-academy-id "q-117579" :question/problem "What is the period of the function $f(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{4x}{3}-{45}^{∘})?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a function in the form $y=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=\\frac{4}{3}.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{(\\frac{4}{3})}={270}^{∘}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329723 :question/answer-fields