to the $x$-axis at $x=-1,$ this root is a simple root (the multiplicity equals $1$).\n\n- Since the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at $x=2,$ this root has even multiplicity.\n\nFrom the given options, the only possible equation is $y=\\frac{1}{10}(x+2{)}^{2}(x+1)(x-2{)}^{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348369 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "433015c8-b02a-5d3b-9bc4-7270edca0b40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}(x+1)(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345929} {:answer/id #uuid "444cadbf-3703-59f5-bad4-46404cc1a695" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{2}(x+1){(x-2)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345940} {:answer/id #uuid "654ada61-08a2-5d34-998b-5c8db9d07e87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}(x+1){(x-2)}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346234} {:answer/id #uuid "6dbb7820-ea22-5b52-910b-269aa2f0dbbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{5}{(x+1)}^{2}(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346310} {:answer/id #uuid "f282e323-500b-5dcf-a254-2d713e281555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=x{(x+1)}^{2}(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "654ada61-08a2-5d34-998b-5c8db9d07e87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={x}^{3}(x+1){(x-2)}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346234} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d5873ca-3084-51bf-9b1d-3de807002492" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347880}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ad55c8cb-7248-5482-9f28-0afc365f8908" :question/math-academy-id "q-80348" :question/problem "![](images/8b/8b086759a25af7e464c0c8be78d36cd4d8458c5c25e7c84cb6ecb28b2d59e9df.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the equation of the polynomial curve shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, 