ent :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348018}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "157e4b00-3d93-51a5-86f8-8df8018840bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-80350" :question/problem "![](images/5e/5e350d9b4db36831eac3ff0708a2acbc903c07265d4c6709632fb8a854121747.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the equation of the polynomial curve shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that the function has precisely three distinct roots, $x=-1$, $x=2$ and $x=5.$\n\nBased on the graph, we can make the following conclusions about the multiplicities of the roots:\n\n- Since the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=-1,$ this root is also a simple root (the multiplicity equals $1$).\n\n- Since the graph passes through $x=2,$ this root has odd multiplicity, and since the graph is tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=2,$ the multiplicity must be greater than one.\n\n- Since the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=5,$ this root is also a simple root (the multiplicity equals $1$).\n\nFrom the given options, the only possible equation is $y=(x+1)(x-2)^{5}(x-5).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b68fad9-861a-5a5d-b8d5-ff1e2fa15ab7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x(x+2)^{7}(x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346430} {:answer/id #uuid "8724b35c-787a-52ef-80ff-eaf99f6a667a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x(x+2)^{5}(x-1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346523} {:answer/id #uuid "94213796-5be7-57ae-81b2-17ed395cf18a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x(x+2)^{3}(x-1)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346645} {:answer/id #uuid "b2ec07fb-d5b8-585e-82ea-e6c5d87d6e70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{x}^{3}(x+2)^{5}(x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346910} {:answer/id #uuid "b5c1df98-76d9-50de-b003-8111fdce77bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{x}^{2}(x+2)(x-1)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94213796-5be7-57ae-81b2-17ed395cf18a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-x(x+2)^{3}(x-1)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346645} :answer-field/id #uuid "db472ae2-2f21-533d-93c0-3a75b3b10cf1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347991}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0154a31e-007f-558f-af24-913ca9813ba7" :question/math-academy-id "q-80352" :question/problem "![](images/19/1956e8c684cc03538877d3ec5d1e72d3d3f48b63341f7739b9a18962b080f1e3.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the equation of the polynomial curve shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that the function has precisely three distinct roots, $x=-2,x=0$ and $x=1.$\n\nBased on the graph, we can make the following conclusions about the multiplicities of the roots:\n\n- Since the graph passes through $x=-2,$ this root has odd multiplicity, and since the graph is tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=-2,$ the multiplicity must be greater than one.\n\n- Since the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=0,$ this root is a simple root (the multiplicity equals $1$).\n\n- Since the graph passes through $x=1,$ this root has odd multiplicity, and since the graph is tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=1,$ the multiplicity must be greater than one.\n\nFrom the given options, the only possible equation is $y=-x(x+2)^{3}(x-1)^{3}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Factored Polynomial Shown in a Graph"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129147 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128963 :question/id #uuid "e158501f-0bac-5d16-956a-59da7f82620f" :question/math-academy-id "e-5818" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7dc5d6aa3a8afed8ebcf49b6d884eee8a443bc759367b624bc7a92cfae515863.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y = (x+2)(x+1)^2(x-2)?$" :question/worked-solution "Based on the factored equation, we can make the following conclusions about the graph:\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the roots $x=\\pm 2$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at these points. Moreover, because $x=\\pm 2$ are simple roots, the graph must *not* be tangent to the $x$-axis at these points.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=-1$ is $2,$ which is even, the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at this point.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\textbf{I}$  and $\\textbf{III}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is positive, as $x$  approaches $\\infty,$ $y$  approaches  $\\infty.$\n\nOnly graph $\\textbf{III}$ displays this end behavior. Therefore, the correct answer is **$\\textbf{III}$**."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d03ac24f-82a6-5af8-b1b8-9021e521d47a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129681 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cc95e90-e6ba-525f-a83f-104d53e7c3a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{II}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324331} {:answer/id #uuid "575c25ea-3c8f-5214-a7ba-34592633f0a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324696} {:answer/id #uuid "5f507194-bc49-50c1-be1b-2724a39b00c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the given graphs are correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324766} {:answer/id #uuid "d034069a-e837-5cba-8556-7b461bd05448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{III}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325782} {:answer/id #uuid "e393b641-9e73-5ed2-a4cd-a1bc68a62b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{IV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e393b641-9e73-5ed2-a4cd-a1bc68a62b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answ