 point.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\text{I}$ and $\\text{IV}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is negative, as $x$ approaches $\\infty ,$ $y$ approaches $-\\infty .$ Since only graph $\\text{I}$ displays this end behavior, the correct answer is $\\text{I}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326705 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4971ab0f-5ec5-5003-a609-5d0cf402c1a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324569} {:answer/id #uuid "6fa949b0-f597-5aa3-9c71-8403549813b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{III}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324889} {:answer/id #uuid "c4ba91b6-5698-5092-ba30-953615f1d91e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{IV}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325663} {:answer/id #uuid "d733a9c7-582f-5c87-8ffe-2dbdff843439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the given graphs are correct" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325842} {:answer/id #uuid "e36393d5-52ce-50a1-81a7-c73a90fc7d56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{II}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4971ab0f-5ec5-5003-a609-5d0cf402c1a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324569} :answer-field/id #uuid "de404b27-a713-5cbf-9bd5-187346f817ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326626}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72df582a-bd3a-59c2-a7b1-3fd49a2aeb61" :question/math-academy-id "q-38631" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f801d9b46aa43cb1065c2935513aee7cc0e448378423735c05ec6df7da89ff8d.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=(x+2)(x+1)^{2}(x-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "Based on the factored equ